enters	one
regulated	one
exempt	one
land_subject	one
enjoys	one
submits	one
# "property" in enters (the securing and regulating of property) and in regulated (the property of his land) could be read as Locke's broad sense (lives, liberties and estates) versus ownership of land.
# But S3 ties them directly ("his land, whose property is to be regulated"), so both mean possessions. P1 is therefore not a bridge.
# "free" in S4 (a free person, free possessions) does not occur in any claim used more than once.
